1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,800
This supplier's bank account… is one of your employees'. An indicator to review, not an accusation.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:11,800
Why it slips: suppliers and employees sit in separate files. Audits test payments, not master data. And the bank details changed a week before the payments.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:24,000
SEG matches supplier accounts against payroll. Same IBAN, ending four-four-one-seven. Changed seven days before three payments. The change log is the evidence. Illustrative test data.

4
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:28,800
The control: two-person approval for any supplier bank change, and segregation of duties.

5
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:34,000
Standard Enterprise Governance, the platform that audits itself. seg-audit.com.
